{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508287-can-a-gangrel-ghoul-mutate-during-a-frenzy","id":1508287,"title":"Can a Gangrel ghoul mutate during a frenzy?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-13T11:28:16-07:00","id":1508287,"title":"Can a Gangrel ghoul mutate during a frenzy?","content":"If all ghouls acquire a weaker version of their master's ( or main Vitae source, anyway ) clan weakness, then may a gangrel ghoul developes animal changes like a Gangrel?<br /> Mabye very slowly ( once every twenty frenzies or more ), or only tiny changes ( much less pronounced than vampire's changes ), or mabye only if the ghoul feed from gangrel's vitae for a very long time.<br /> <br /> Additional question, could a ghoul <i>deliberately</i> induce those changes if he has a secured place and an unlimited supply of Vitae? ( es. feeding every night, keeping all his blood turned into Vitae all the time, deliberately frenzies countless times )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-13T11:58:47-07:00","id":1508288,"title":"","content":"Which rules are you using?<br /> <br /> The V20 ghouls expanded rules has Clan weakness for Ghouls that represent how that blood manifests in still mortal bodies; Gangrel ghouls get the Lunacy Flaw rather than taking on physical characteristics.of animals.<br /> <br /> That said, I'm not sure how a ghoul locked away in comfortable seclusion of their own making, with limitless vitae on hand, is supposed o be Frenzying constantly. They need to rile their lesser Beast up, not make it happy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-13T13:00:37-07:00","id":1508290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That said, I'm not sure how a ghoul locked away in comfortable seclusion of their own making, with limitless vitae on hand, is supposed o be Frenzying constantly. </div> </div> </div>Playing heavy metal, working at the heavy bag, focusing on his own frustrations... self harm, mabye, or even doing drugs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-13T14:46:58-07:00","id":1508301,"title":"","content":"The Frenzy rules are very clear that if you're in control of the situation, it should drastically reduce the difficulty of resisting Frenzy, or even eliminate the chances all together.<br /> <br /> While V20 G&amp;R does discuss how ghouls are more volatile in many ways thanks to having the full range of human emotions to keep in check compared to a vampire's more muted responses, humans also acclimate. The longer this goes on, the less the ghou's emotions are generally going to get driven to the point of Frenzy. Why Frenzy over something you can stop whenever you want?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-14T00:55:29-07:00","id":1508332,"title":"","content":"Well, actually even normal humans can drive themselves frantic with appropriate dancing, loud music and psychoactive substances. In the RPG Kult there is even a skill to do it ( called &quot;Ecstasy&quot; ).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-14T01:14:53-07:00","id":1508333,"title":"","content":"Ghoul weaknesses are a very inconsistent, arguably tacked on part of VTM. As far as mainline books go, Non-revenant Ghouls don't exhibit bloodline weaknesses at all and it's considered rediculous should Nosferatu ghouls become ugly or Ventrue ghouls become picky. Like for many vampires they want to recruit ghouls to shore up their weaknesses and nothing would stump you harder than the Malkavian getting herself a nurse that's just as crazy as she is. I don't think a Nosferatu's spy network would work half as well if it's main characters were suffering from -nosferatu ghoul face- all the time. <br /> <br /> Ghoul weaknesses come to the forefront in books about ghouls for playing ghoul campaigns, to make the book bigger and your coterie more diverse. They exist purely for non-diegetic reasons. So with that in mind... do what you want, or more specifically, it might be a cool idea in a Ghoul or even hunter game but it wouldn't work so well for vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-14T02:58:24-07:00","id":1508347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508287-can-a-gangrel-ghoul-mutate-during-a-frenzy?p=1508332#post1508332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, actually even normal humans can drive themselves frantic with appropriate dancing, loud music and psychoactive substances. In the RPG Kult there is even a skill to do it ( called &quot;Ecstasy&quot; ).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm very well aware of ecstatic meditative practices. The things about them are:<br /> <br /> 1) They can take hours to get a person into a specific mental state.<br /> 2) The aren't actually fugue states were people can't knock themselves out of it if they want to stop (aka the &quot;in control&quot; aspect remains).<br /> 3) They don't necessarily produce the necessary emotional states to trigger Frenzy.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, the idea doesn't really work RAW anyway, and so if you really want to do it, you're going to be in house-rules territory anyway. To me, it seems like a lot of work for nothing, because it just means Gangrel are going to have to kill their ghouls regularly as they get too physically weird to be around humans over time to fulfill their purpose of being able to handle their domitor's need during the day and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}